[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186165033 :answer-field/choices 17592186165034] [:db/retract 17592186165033 :answer-field/choices 17592186165035] [:db/retract 17592186165033 :answer-field/choices 17592186165036] [:db/retract 17592186165033 :answer-field/choices 17592186165037] [:db/retract 17592186165033 :answer-field/choices 17592186165038] {:db/id 17592186166968 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e8cf80bf-23f2-50e5-8be6-fd421cafc0d7" "question-7ecead24-f472-509d-9b09-182eae6554e7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e8cf80bf-23f2-50e5-8be6-fd421cafc0d7" :question/id #uuid "e8cf80bf-23f2-50e5-8be6-fd421cafc0d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-346662" :question/problem "Let $C=\\{-3,-1,1,3\\}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${1}_{C}(-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the indicator function ${1}_{C}(x)$ of a set $C$ equals $1$ if $x\\in C$ and $0$ if $x\\notin C.$ This can be written using Iverson bracket notation as\n\n$$\n{1}_{C}(x)=1[x\\in C].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{1}_{C}(-1)=1[-1\\in C]=1[-1\\in \\{-3,-1,1,3\\}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8c55f3e7-608f-546e-9238-bec098222d4f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8c55f3e7-608f-546e-9238-bec098222d4f" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c55f3e7-608f-546e-9238-bec098222d4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c77659db-76b7-535a-9c58-254c1f6de06a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7a42e783-06ac-540f-a993-5fee32a5d1a7" "answer-c77659db-76b7-535a-9c58-254c1f6de06a" "answer-905baf65-bc02-52ab-a96c-06c275629272" "answer-c64a4829-6ad8-5110-9db6-5fd9a585d15a" "answer-d3d06cfb-9a89-5639-8808-7411f0dd598c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a42e783-06ac-540f-a993-5fee32a5d1a7" :answer/id #uuid "7a42e783-06ac-540f-a993-5fee32a5d1a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1[-1=C]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c77659db-76b7-535a-9c58-254c1f6de06a" :answer/id #uuid "c77659db-76b7-535a-9c58-254c1f6de06a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1[-1\\in \\{-3,-1,1,3\\}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-905baf65-bc02-52ab-a96c-06c275629272" :answer/id #uuid "905baf65-bc02-52ab-a96c-06c275629272" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1[-1\\notin \\{-3,-1,1,3\\}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c64a4829-6ad8-5110-9db6-5fd9a585d15a" :answer/id #uuid "c64a4829-6ad8-5110-9db6-5fd9a585d15a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1[C\\in \\{-3,-1,1,3\\}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3d06cfb-9a89-5639-8808-7411f0dd598c" :answer/id #uuid "d3d06cfb-9a89-5639-8808-7411f0dd598c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1[\\{-3,-1,1,3\\}\\in -1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7ecead24-f472-509d-9b09-182eae6554e7" :question/id #uuid "7ecead24-f472-509d-9b09-182eae6554e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-346663" :question/problem "Let $D=\\{0,5,10\\}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${1}_{D}(7)?$" :question/worked-solution "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the indicator function ${1}_{D}(x)$ of a set $D$ equals $1$ if $x\\in D$ and $0$ if $x\\notin D.$ This can be written using Iverson bracket notation as\n\n$$\n{1}_{D}(x)=1[x\\in D].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{1}_{D}(7)=1[7\\in D]=1[7\\in \\{0,5,10\\}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cd8b1eb9-905f-5eaa-b94d-45d4a5b08f18"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cd8b1eb9-905f-5eaa-b94d-45d4a5b08f18" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd8b1eb9-905f-5eaa-b94d-45d4a5b08f18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-929abffe-450c-5006-a4e0-9188f9b6910d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3e5a4ce9-38a3-50c2-ab37-2b31fa255565" "answer-929abffe-450c-5006-a4e0-9188f9b6910d" "answer-caeec9e3-866d-5050-ab7c-4b6736d7497b" "answer-3f98e784-15fe-5da6-bf43-5d7bde990e34" "answer-34d52dde-78fc-56d2-a22f-16743942f394"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e5a4ce9-38a3-50c2-ab37-2b31fa255565" :answer/id #uuid "3e5a4ce9-38a3-50c2-ab37-2b31fa255565" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1[7=D]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-929abffe-450c-5006-a4e0-9188f9b6910d" :answer/id #uuid "929abffe-450c-5006-a4e0-9188f9b6910d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1[7\\in \\{0,5,10\\}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caeec9e3-866d-5050-ab7c-4b6736d7497b" :answer/id #uuid "caeec9e3-866d-5050-ab7c-4b6736d7497b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1[7\\notin \\{0,5,10\\}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f98e784-15fe-5da6-bf43-5d7bde990e34" :answer/id #uuid "3f98e784-15fe-5da6-bf43-5d7bde990e34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1[D\\in \\{0,5,10\\}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34d52dde-78fc-56d2-a22f-16743942f394" :answer/id #uuid "34d52dde-78fc-56d2-a22f-16743942f394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1[\\{0,5,10\\}\\in 7]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166969 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f030361e-8a29-5e63-bca8-4e28e1ba5da0" "question-e3d61585-203e-5ae2-ba7d-32b154b3cecc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f030361e-8a29-5e63-bca8-4e28e1ba5da0" :question/id #uuid "f030361e-8a29-5e63-bca8-4e28e1ba5da0" :question/math-academy-id "q-346677" :question/problem "$$\n{x}_{1}=9,\\,{x}_{2}=-8,\\,{x}_{3}=-1,\\,{x}_{4}=4,\\,{x}_{5}=2\n$$\n\nGiven the values ${x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3},\\,{x}_{4},\\,{x}_{5}$ above, we have\n\n${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i}=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression $1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i}$ equals ${x}_{i}$ when ${x}_{i}>0$ and equals $0$ otherwise. Thus, the sum \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i}\n$$\n\nadds up only the positive values.\n\nWe evaluate the indicator function for each ${x}_{i}:$\n\n- $1[{x}_{1}>0]=1[9>0]=1$\n\n- $1[{x}_{2}>0]=1[-8>0]=0$\n\n- $1[{x}_{3}>0]=1[-1>0]=0$\n\n- $1[{x}_{4}>0]=1[4>0]=1$\n\n- $1[{x}_{5}>0]=1[2>0]=1$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i} & =1\\cdot 9+0\\cdot (-8)+0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =9+0+0+4+2 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-034b7137-7dce-507f-82b0-3f725c6f8c4a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-034b7137-7dce-507f-82b0-3f725c6f8c4a" :answer-field/id #uuid "034b7137-7dce-507f-82b0-3f725c6f8c4a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-156a71be-c9a4-5ae7-9a2c-02e2f98c3a59" :answer-field/choices ["answer-156a71be-c9a4-5ae7-9a2c-02e2f98c3a59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-156a71be-c9a4-5ae7-9a2c-02e2f98c3a59" :answer/id #uuid "156a71be-c9a4-5ae7-9a2c-02e2f98c3a59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e3d61585-203e-5ae2-ba7d-32b154b3cecc" :question/id #uuid "e3d61585-203e-5ae2-ba7d-32b154b3cecc" :question/math-academy-id "q-347438" :question/problem "$$\n{x}_{1}=-6,\\,{x}_{2}=-1,\\,{x}_{3}=0,\\,{x}_{4}=4,\\,{x}_{5}=7\n$$\n\nGiven the values ${x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3},\\,{x}_{4},\\,{x}_{5}$ above, we have\n\n${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}\\ge 0]\\cdot (2{x}_{i})+1[{x}_{i}<0]\\cdot 1=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression $1[{x}_{i}\\ge 0]\\cdot (2{x}_{i})+1[{x}_{i}<0]\\cdot 1$ equals $2{x}_{i}$ when ${x}_{i}\\ge 0$ and equals $1$ when ${x}_{i}<0.$ Thus, the sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}\\ge 0]\\cdot (2{x}_{i})+1[{x}_{i}<0]\\cdot 1\n$$\n\nadds $2{x}_{i}$ for nonnegative values and $1$ for negative values.\n\nWe evaluate the indicator function for each ${x}_{i}:$\n\n- $1[{x}_{1}\\ge 0]=1[-6\\ge 0]=0,$ $1[{x}_{1}<0]=1$\n\n- $1[{x}_{2}\\ge 0]=1[-1\\ge 0]=0,$ $1[{x}_{2}<0]=1$\n\n- $1[{x}_{3}\\ge 0]=1[0\\ge 0]=1,$ $1[{x}_{3}<0]=0$\n\n- $1[{x}_{4}\\ge 0]=1[4\\ge 0]=1,$ $1[{x}_{4}<0]=0$\n\n- $1[{x}_{5}\\ge 0]=1[7\\ge 0]=1,$ $1[{x}_{5}<0]=0$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}\\ge 0]\\cdot (2{x}_{i})+1[{x}_{i}<0]\\cdot 1 & =1+1+2\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =1+1+0+8+14 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-edb32b44-fa3a-53b5-9c67-b4cbe35e057e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-edb32b44-fa3a-53b5-9c67-b4cbe35e057e" :answer-field/id #uuid "edb32b44-fa3a-53b5-9c67-b4cbe35e057e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-dd697bf3-bab3-5be7-93b9-af592dc078ba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dd697bf3-bab3-5be7-93b9-af592dc078ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd697bf3-bab3-5be7-93b9-af592dc078ba" :answer/id #uuid "dd697bf3-bab3-5be7-93b9-af592dc078ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167304 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{2,4,6,8\\}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to $1[5\\in B]?$" :question/worked-solution "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of a set $A$ equals $1$ if $x\\in A$ and $0$ if $x\\notin A.$ This can be written using Iverson bracket notation as\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=1[x\\in A].\n$$\n\nHere, the Iverson bracket expression $1[5\\in B]$ has $x=5$ and $A=B.$ Therefore, converting back to set indicator notation, we have\n\n$$\n1[5\\in B]={1}_{B}(5).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186165033 :answer-field/correct "answer-fd7b8b0c-b17c-5fc2-aad1-cf9ecfd4c52f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6acf5d37-f233-58a7-b644-4950c5f08b96" "answer-23fcb709-e1df-5686-a023-45de9c7332ca" "answer-fd7b8b0c-b17c-5fc2-aad1-cf9ecfd4c52f" "answer-6ec50b2b-0fb1-535c-bee6-07f2da381e05" "answer-0e9e8e21-b550-5dab-acbe-bf94504b1d71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6acf5d37-f233-58a7-b644-4950c5f08b96" :answer/id #uuid "6acf5d37-f233-58a7-b644-4950c5f08b96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1}_{5}(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23fcb709-e1df-5686-a023-45de9c7332ca" :answer/id #uuid "23fcb709-e1df-5686-a023-45de9c7332ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1}_{5}(B)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd7b8b0c-b17c-5fc2-aad1-cf9ecfd4c52f" :answer/id #uuid "fd7b8b0c-b17c-5fc2-aad1-cf9ecfd4c52f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1}_{B}(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ec50b2b-0fb1-535c-bee6-07f2da381e05" :answer/id #uuid "6ec50b2b-0fb1-535c-bee6-07f2da381e05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1}_{B}(6)" 